<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.13.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00293</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.13.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>90ed58af-5aa5-49ff-9645-16b046fe7f17</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="practice">
  <exercise id="d746e47d-1480-40ae-a4c4-5f0f9911c402" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the slope of the line that goes through the points in the given table of values?</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <tgroup cols="5"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis></entry><entry>1</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>3</entry>
            <entry>4</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>\(y\)</emphasis></entry><entry>6</entry>
            <entry>11</entry>
            <entry>16</entry>
            <entry>21</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! Since the change in \(y\) is 5, and the change in \(x\)is 1, the slope is \(\frac51\) or 5.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 1.13.2 and 1.13.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 5. You seem to be stuck. Who can you ask for help?
     </para></solution></exercise>
     <exercise id="_5b06c140-6d95-47bd-ae33-47e2866404fd" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>In the equation, \(y = 4x + 2\), what is the value of the \(y\)-intercept?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! In the form, \(y=mx +b\), \(b\) is the \(y\)-intercept so 2 is the \(y\)-intercept in this equation.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.13.1.</para><para>The correct answer is 2. You seem to be stuck. Who can you ask for help?
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="f32865f8-862f-40d1-b4c1-fc95f906f760" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Identify the slope in the given graph.</para>
      
    </problem>
    <solution><para>Correct! From the point \((-1,1)\) to \((0,4)\), the slope is 3.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.13.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 3. You seem to be stuck. Who can you ask for help?
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_67f9fa7e-8472-4e31-867a-fd8a46226ea4" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which of the following is an equation for the table of values?</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <tgroup cols="5"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis></entry><entry>0</entry>
            <entry>1</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>3</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>\(y\)</emphasis></entry><entry>2</entry>
            <entry>7</entry>
            <entry>12</entry>
            <entry>17</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
    <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(y=2x+5\)</para><para>\(y=5x+2\)</para><para>\(y=7x-2\)</para><para>\(y=5x-2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(y\)-intercept is 2 and the slope is 5.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 1.13.2 and 1.13.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(y=5x+2\). You seem to be stuck. Who can you ask for help?</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_02f87ef5-ff24-4d92-8448-0da1ee9d0ea0" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For the equation \(y= -2x +3\), what is the value when \(x = 2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! Substitute \(x=2\) so that \(y = -2(2)+3= -4+3=-1\).</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.13.4.</para><para>The correct answer is -1. You seem to be stuck. Who can you ask for help?
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_096276e4-4e51-45b3-8b2b-014cfb1ee59f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Jonah started the month with $40 and earned $15 each week walking dogs for neighbors. How much does he have after \(w\)  weeks?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(y=15w +40\)</para><para>\(y=40w\)</para><para>\(y=40w+15\)</para><para>\(y=40(15w)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! Jonah started with $40 so that is the \(y\)-intercept. He earned $15 each week so that is the slope.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 1.13.2 and 1.13.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(y=15w +40\). You seem to be stuck. Who can you ask for help?

     </para></solution></exercise>
     <exercise id="d7acd21e-9f2a-4b1a-aa74-1130083fb59b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Write the slope of the given table.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <tgroup cols="4"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis></entry><entry>0</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>4</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>\(y\)</emphasis></entry><entry>5</entry>
            <entry>11</entry>
            <entry>17</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The change in \(y\) is 6 and the change in \(x\) is 2 so the slope is \(\frac62\) or 3.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 1.13.2 and 1.13.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 3. You seem to be stuck. Who can you ask for help?
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_6f2232f8-366d-46a3-bb45-08649f2af71b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For the equation \(g=\frac{w+3}{2}\), what is the value of \(g\) when \(w=7\)?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 5</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.13.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 5. You seem to be stuck. Who can you ask for help?
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_2af60583-92e1-4fe3-a3e7-418324146104" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Identify the \(y\)-intercept of the given table.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <tgroup cols="4"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis></entry><entry>1</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>3</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>\(y\)</emphasis></entry><entry>3</entry>
            <entry>5</entry>
            <entry>7</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! Work backward using the pattern to when \(x =0\). Subtract 1 from \(x=1\) and subtract 2 from \(x=3\).</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.13.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 1. You seem to be stuck. Who can you ask for help?
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="a0a731c8-f232-4ed5-8701-2a23e8395c7e" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Identify the slope of the line between \((3, 6)\) and \((-2, 7)\).</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(- \frac15\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.13.1.</para><para>The correct answer is \(- \frac15\). You seem to be stuck. Who can you ask for help?
     </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
